{
  "analysis": "I found the bug! In the `step()` function, the trace code uses `pc` before it's declared with `const pc = this.pc;`. This causes a ReferenceError due to JavaScript's temporal dead zone, but the error output isn't showing because of buffering with the timeout/redirect. I need to move the trace code after the `const pc` declaration and add a startup print.",
  "plan": "Fix the `step()` function by moving the trace code after `const pc = this.pc;`. Add a startup console.error to verify the VM starts. Then re-run with output to a file.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "python3 - <<'PY'
src=open('/app/vm.js').read()
# Remove the broken trace code before const pc
old = r'''  step() {
    // Trace fwrite calls
    if ((pc >>> 0) === 0x43a950 && this.instCount < 100000) {
      console.error(`[trace] fwrite called r4=${this.r[4]>>>0} r5=${this.r[5]>>>0} r6=${this.r[6]>>>0} r7=${this.r[7]>>>0} ra=${(this.r[31]>>>0).toString(16)} inst=${this.instCount}`);
    }
    if (this.maxInst && this.instCount >= this.maxInst) { this.running = false; return; }
    const pc = this.pc;
    const inst = this.mem.readU32(pc);
    this.execute(inst, pc);
    this.instCount++;
  }'''
new = r'''  step() {
    if (this.maxInst && this.instCount >= this.maxInst) { this.running = false; return; }
    const pc = this.pc;
    // Trace fwrite calls
    if ((pc >>> 0) === 0x43a950 && this.instCount < 100000) {
      console.error(`[trace] fwrite called r4=${this.r[4]>>>0} r5=${this.r[5]>>>0} r6=${this.r[6]>>>0} r7=${this.r[7]>>>0} ra=${(this.r[31]>>>0).toString(16)} inst=${this.instCount}`);
    }
    const inst = this.mem.readU32(pc);
    this.execute(inst, pc);
    this.instCount++;
  }'''
src = src.replace(old, new)
# Add startup print
src = src.replace("function main() {", "function main() {\n  console.error('[vm] starting...');")
open('/app/vm.js','w').write(src)
PY
node -c /app/vm.js
",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "rm -f /tmp/frame.bmp /tmp/vm_out.txt; timeout 10 node /app/vm.js > /tmp/vm_out.txt 2>&1; echo "exit=$?"; wc -l /tmp/vm_out.txt; head -60 /tmp/vm_out.txt; ls -la /tmp/frame.bmp 2>/dev/null
",
      "duration": 12.0
    }
  ]
}
